+The <src> ref is stored at the remote only if
 <dst> does not exist, or <dst> is a proper subset (i.e. an
 ancestor) of <src>.  This check, known as "fast-forward check",
 is performed to avoid accidentally overwriting the
 remote ref and losing other peoples' commits from there.
 
-With `--force`, the fast-forward check is disabled for all refs.
-
-Optionally, a <ref> parameter can be prefixed with a plus '+' sign
-to disable the fast-forward check only on that ref.
+This build of Git does not allow the check to be skipped: the
+`--force` option and a leading `+` on a <ref> are ignored.
 
